<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    "Aircraft of the day". Two cells by one by default: one airframe is a
    smaller fact than a route, and the short compact layout (AircraftWidget)
    carries all of it in two lines — the airframe, the date, the type code,
    the range, the flown status as a dot. Resizable to four cells, which adds
    the runway figure and states the status in words, and to two rows, which
    is the challenge card's three-band layout with an empty band where that
    card draws its map.

    The width floor is the challenge widget's 140dp, deliberately: the two
    widgets share a slot, and a floor above what a launcher's two cells
    measure (One UI: 176–184dp) is a widget that cannot be made two cells wide
    at all. One UI derives the picker's column count from minWidth as well —
    176dp listed as 3×1 — so minWidth cannot be raised to what the layout
    needs (about 174dp) without losing the two-cell default. Its picker also
    draws every preview at 0.83 of the grid, in dp, without scaling the
    content, so the two-cell preview there clips the range chip's last glyph;
    the widget itself, at a real 176dp, does not. The height floor is 40dp — not what the short layout needs (about
    80dp) but what a launcher needs to *hear* "one row": One UI sizes the
    picker entry by the classic 70n − 30 formula, so anything above 40dp is
    listed and placed as two rows and targetCellHeight is ignored. A real
    one-row grant is around 100dp (One UI: 102dp), which the short layout
    fits with room.

    updatePeriodMillis is 0 because the widget is refreshed by a wall-clock
    alarm at local midnight (MidnightRefresh.AIRCRAFT), not by polling. There is
    no previewImage: Android 15 takes a rendered preview from the widget itself
    (PublishWidgetPreview), so a hand-drawn one would only go stale.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="140dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="140dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="40dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="360dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="260dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:description="@string/widget_aircraft_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout" />
